-- title:
--   Virtually torsion-free even away-unit groups at q
-- statement:
--   **Numerical data.** $N$, $q$, $q'$ are natural numbers with $N$ nonzero and squarefree (`hN`), $q$ and $q'$ prime, neither dividing $N$ (`hqN`, `hq'N`), $q' \neq q$ (`hqq'`), and $5 \le q$, $5 \le q'$ (`hq5`, `hq'5`); $D$ is a nonzero natural number divisible by $2Nqq'$ (`hD`).
--
--   **Valuation data at $q$.** $A_2$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit (`hA₂`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$ acts by isometries for its valuation (`hiso₂`), and $v_2$ is a height-one prime of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ containing $q$ (`hv₂`).
--
--   **The definite quaternion algebra and its orders.** For rationals $a_1,b_1$, the hypothesis `hdef₁` says $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and that for a height-one prime $v$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element a unit) exactly when $v$ contains $q'$. Here $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order (an order maximal among orders, where an order is a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, and $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning the algebra), $R_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders whose additive relative index in the first is $N$ (`hR₁`), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`). The finite-adelic unit $n_1$ lies in `primeHeckeSet R₁ q` (`hn₁`): $n_1$ lies in the finite-adelic box of $R_1$, $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lies in that box, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not. Writing $S_1 = R_1 \sqcap \mathrm{conj}_{n_1}(R_1)$ for `meetOrder R₁ n₁`, the hypotheses require: $S_1$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq$ (`hS₁`); $S_1$ is stable under conjugation by $n_1$ (`hnorm₁`); shifting twice by $n_1$ on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of $S_1$ is the identity (`hsq₁`); the class sets of the stabilisers of $S_1$ and of $R_1$ are finite; and `hlaws₁` holds, the four Hecke laws `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q Λ₁ R₁ n₁` asserting that the edge Hecke matrices pairwise commute, that the vertex Hecke matrices pairwise commute, that for primes $\ell \neq q$ the two degeneracy pushforwards intertwine edge and vertex Hecke matrices, and that the joint kernel of the two degeneracy maps is preserved by the edge Hecke matrices.
--
--   **The indefinite algebra.** For rationals $a,b$, the hypothesis `hB` says $0<a$ or $0<b$, and that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`).
--
--   **The characteristic-zero moduli tower.** $\overline{F}$ is a field extension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (principal divisors exist and have degree zero, all residue fields of places are finite over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\Omega_{\overline F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ is free of rank one) and is essentially of finite type. $X$ is a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $D$ via $\pi_X$, $\bar s$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of that base, and `pt` assigns to each ring $S$, each $S$-point $s$ of the base and each fake elliptic curve of type $(\Lambda,N)$ over $S$ a section of $\pi_X$ over $s$. The hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` are the four coarse-moduli clauses for `pt` (invariance under isomorphism; compatibility with base change along ring maps and pullback of fake elliptic curves; surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields), without the universal property. $\mathfrak{M}$ is a curve model of $\overline F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $e_{\mathfrak M}$ is an isomorphism from its total space to the fibre product of $\pi_X$ and $\bar s$ with $e_{\mathfrak M}$ followed by the second projection equal to $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`he𝔐`), `gal` is a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to the semilinear automorphisms of $\overline F$, $\mathbb{T}$ is tower data over $\overline F$ for the primes away from $q,q'$, `galT` the corresponding Galois actions on the tower fields, and $W$, $WT$ are pairs of semilinear automorphisms of $\overline F$ and of the tower fields. The hypothesis `tw` is a witness of type `ModuliTowerWitnessD` for these data: it provides fake elliptic curves (with extra level, on the tower fields) attached to places, bijectively up to isomorphism, compatibly with `pt` and $e_{\mathfrak M}$, with the Galois actions `gal`, `galT` restricting to the given automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $W$, $WT$ acting trivially on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and with the degeneracy and Atkin–Lehner comparisons of the tower.
--
--   **The $q$-adic matrix realisation.** $\iota_2$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map from $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ to $2\times 2$ matrices over [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13), the closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $A_2$ for its valuation; $\rho_2$ is the induced homomorphism from the unit group of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ to $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over that field (`hρ₂`). $\varpi_2$ is a pseudo-uniformiser of that field inside the completion whose image is $q$ (`hϖ₂`), and the ring `HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` of functions holomorphic on every affinoid of the upper half-plane is a domain (`hdom₂`).
--
--   **Hecke elements away from $q,q'$.** For each prime $\ell \neq q,q'$, $s_2(\ell)$ is a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ and $s\!f_2(\ell)$ a finite-adelic unit; `hs₂` requires four things: at every height-one prime not containing $q$ the component of $s\!f_2(\ell)$ is $s_2(\ell)\otimes 1$; at primes containing $q$ it is $1$; the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s\!f_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` if $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise; and the reduced norm of $s_2(\ell)$ is $\ell$.
--
--   **The groups.** $\Gamma_2$ assigns a subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ to each object of the tower index $\mathrm{Option}$. By `hΓ₂0`, $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ consists of the units lying in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` (those whose image in the completion at every height-one prime $w \neq v_2$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$) whose reduced norm has even $q$-adic valuation. By `hΓ₂ℓ`, for each prime $\ell \neq q,q'$, $\Gamma_2(\ell)$ is the intersection of $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ with its image under conjugation by $s_2(\ell)$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner elements.** The hypothesis `hw₂` gives $w_2(\mathrm{none}) \in$ `awayUnits R₁ v₂` of reduced norm $q$, and for each $\ell$ an element $w_2(\ell) \in$ `awayUnits (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) v₂` of reduced norm $q$. The hypothesis `hwbar₂` gives $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$ of reduced norm $q'$ whose local image at every prime $u \neq v_2$ not containing $q'$ lies in the local unit box of $R_1$, and conjugation by which preserves the local boxes of $R_1$ and of $\Lambda_1$ at every $u \neq v_2$; and, for each $\ell$, the analogous element $\bar w_2(\ell)$ with `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)` in place of $R_1$.
--
--   **Local Galois data.** $d\mathrm{Iso}_2$ realises the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ by isometric automorphisms of the completion, acting as the Galois action (`hdIso₂`). The character $\chi$ on that decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathbb{Z}/2$ is trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on every Frobenius element at $q$ (`hχ₂`), and satisfies $\chi(\tau)=1$ if and only if $\tau$ fixes every element $x$ of the residue field of $A_2$ with $x^{q^2}=x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   **Coefficient rings.** $\mathcal{O}_0$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal{O}_0$ is $\pi$-adically complete, its residue ring has exactly $q$ elements, $(q)=(\pi)$, and `ratClosure A₂` is its fraction field. $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero $\mathcal{O}_0$-domain with an $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element integral over $\mathcal{O}_0$ modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo it, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{q}$ modulo it. Further, $v\mathrm{det}$ measures the determinant valuation, $v\mathrm{det}(g) = \mathrm{ofAdd}\,n$ holding precisely when $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_0$ times $\pi^{n}$ (`hvdet`); $\psi_0 : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to$ completion takes values in the valuation-$\le 1$ locus and agrees with the structural maps on $\mathcal{O}_0$ (`hψ₀`, `hψ₀𝒪`); the image of $\pi$ is $\varpi_2$ (`hπϖ`), $N$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_0$ (`hN₀`), the image of $\mathcal{O}_0$ is exactly the valuation-$\le 1$ locus of `ratClosure A₂` (`h𝒪₀`), and the valuation has rank one in the sense of `hrk`.
--
--   **Integral models, degeneracies and Atkin–Lehner maps.** $\mathcal{X}_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ with `pt₀` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of type $(\Lambda,N)$ in the full sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (the four clauses above together with the universal property), $\mathcal{X}_0$ being integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell \neq q,q'$, $\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ with $\mathrm{ptT}_0(\ell)$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with extra level $\ell$. The maps $d_{0}(\ell), d_{1}(\ell) : \mathcal{Y}_0(\ell) \to \mathcal{X}_0$ lie over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) and induce on moduli points the forgetting of the extra level (`hd₀`) and the passage along a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`). The maps $\mathrm{ar}, \overline{\mathrm{ar}} : \mathcal{X}_0 \to \mathcal{X}_0$ lie over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) and induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q$ and at $q'$ respectively on moduli points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.** $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ map, for $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with the Deligne functor $\Omega$ of the formal upper half-plane over `ratClosure A₂` to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hCD` is a conjunction of twelve clauses, summarised here: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$ in $B$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action (Frobenius twist by $-v\mathrm{det}$ on the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-coordinate together with pullback of the Deligne datum) of the elements of `awayUnits R₁ v₂`, and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under that of the intersection of `awayUnits R₁ v₂` with its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$; surjectivity on nilpotent points over algebraically closed fields with fibres exactly the orbits of those twisted actions, for $\Theta$ and for each $\Theta T(\ell)$; the universal property of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$ among invariant natural families; the compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_{0}(\ell)$ and, via the twisted action of $s_2(\ell)$, with $d_{1}(\ell)$; and the identification of $\mathrm{ar}$ with the Frobenius twist by $1$ on the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-coordinate and of $\overline{\mathrm{ar}}$ with the twisted action of $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two assertions hold.
--
--   First, there is a subgroup $\Gamma''$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ with $\Gamma'' \le \Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$, with `Γ''.relIndex (Γ₂ none) ≠ 0` (so $\Gamma''$ has finite index in $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$), and such that every element of finite order in the image $\rho_2(\Gamma'') \le \mathrm{PGL}_2$ over [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) equals $1$; that is, $\rho_2(\Gamma'')$ is torsion-free.
--
--   Second, for every prime $\ell$ distinct from $q$ and $q'$ there is a subgroup $\Gamma''$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ with $\Gamma'' \le \Gamma_2(\ell)$, with nonzero relative index in $\Gamma_2(\ell)$, and such that every element of finite order in $\rho_2(\Gamma'')$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the virtual torsion-freeness input to the $q$-adic uniformisation step: inside the Čerednik–Drinfeld frame it produces, for the even part of the away-from-$v_2$ unit group of the Eichler order and for each of its level-$\ell$ congruence intersections, a finite-index subgroup whose image in $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over the closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ in the completion at $A_2$ is torsion-free, the condition under which Mumford's theory of $p$-adic uniformisation applies. It is used by the statement producing the Mumford embedding of the Shimura curve tower from the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
